{
  "title": "Integer.parseInt crashes on empty loyalty string for planeswalkers",
  "description": "Regression from 3fd7c6f30a.\n\
\n\
`BridgeGameStateBuilder.java:84` calls `Integer.parseInt(perm.getLoyalty())` \
but `getLoyalty()` returns `\"\"` when a planeswalker has no counters in its \
map. This throws `NumberFormatException`.\n\
\n\
`CardView` only sets loyalty from counters when `getCounters(game) != null && \
!getCounters(game).isEmpty()` (line 483). Otherwise loyalty stays at default \
`\"\"`.\n\
\n\
Both players hit this at 23:03:30 in game_20260325_225154. Cascaded into a \
Gemini 400 error from the corrupted tool response.\n\
\n\
Source: BridgeGameStateBuilder.java:84\n\
\n\
Fix: `loyalty.isEmpty() ? 0 : Integer.parseInt(loyalty)` — 0 is the correct \
semantic value for an empty loyalty string.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 1,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "bridge",
  ],
  "created_at": "2026-03-25T23:30:00.000000-07:00",
  "updated_at": "2026-03-25T23:30:00.000000-07:00",
}
